exercises.prompt:
Given:
type Result = { type: 'success'; data: Movie[] } | { type: 'error'; message: string }

Inside a switch on result.type, TypeScript knows the exact shape in each case. What pattern is this called?

exercises.code:
interface Movie { title: string; poster: string | null }

function getPoster(movie: Movie): string {
  // your code here
}

exercises.answer:
interface Movie { title: string; poster: string | null }

function getPoster(movie: Movie): string {
  if (movie.poster !== null) {
    return movie.poster
  }
  return '/placeholder.jpg'
}
